Z||000000||gkozlov||07-15-2000||07:52 PM||||I found a 86 SE auto with 114K miles. It has pw, sunroof, pm, ac, rear deck release, and factory wing. The car appears to be average to good condition except it has a knock when engine is revved. It does not knock when at idle. The owner tells me its a piston and risk? pin???? Does this sound correct? I am not mechanically inclined at all. The engine oil seemed clean. And the car started up and ran. Asking price is $650.<BR>What should I do? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||07-15-2000||08:10 PM||||$650 is not a bad price, try to talk the owner down a little. It sounds like you will need to rebuild the engine. The owner is speaking about the piston and wrist pin. The wrist pin is a rod that attaches the piston to the connecting rod, which is attached to the crank. Its possible. A solid sounding knock most often means rebuild time.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 07-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowCG||07-15-2000||09:27 PM||||Yup,start at "$300 cash",and take it from there.<BR>Might also be a rod knock,but at that point it still needs a motor.<BR>At least it runs so you can see what works,and what doesn't;more opportunity to go down on the price!||||reg||1
